& [RuntimeRootAndTransitionContract] is implemented
  + RuntimeSnapshot binds one immutable DeterministicRuntimeRoot to its canonical SHA-256 digest
  + the root pins exact runtime and CTPR versions, policies, limits, logical clock, forms, repository, Calendar, Planner, and trace
  + RuntimeOperation is a strict closed tagged union with unique operation identity, caller, expected root digest, and narrower declared limits
  + evaluation returns either boxed successor plus RuntimeReceipt or RuntimeFault with no partial successor
  + receipts bind before and after digest, operation, caller, kind, logical time, emitted identities, trace, limits, disposition, and typed output
  + faults bind kind, operation, subjects, expected, observed, evidence, safe residual, and trace location

& [FakeRepositoryAndMateriality] are deterministic projections
  + compare-and-append validates exact branch head, predecessor set, repository identity, unique records, content bytes and digest, event input and digest, event frontier, optional snapshot, and normalized CTPR graph
  + explicit branch creation and multi-predecessor merge use named branch heads and present predecessor generations
  + accepted state retains content bytes, generations, events, snapshots, branch heads, and a deterministically rebuilt subject and content index
  + root reconstruction revalidates content, event, snapshot, and generation digests and repository/snapshot frontier agreement
  + classification applies one exact MaterialityPolicy revision to return capture, aggregate, or omit with the matched rule and evidence
  + classification never edits prior history or admits its candidate as an event

& [LogicalCalendarAndPlanner] preserve distinctions
  + LogicalClock advances only through an accepted positive caller-supplied delta
  + Calendar revision checks exact predecessor identity and ordinary revisions cannot smuggle a lifecycle transition
  + lifecycle evaluation checks exact latest revision and supplied logical tick, applies a closed transition table, and emits a typed material-event candidate without admission or action
  + recurrence retains immutable revision history and applies supplied candidate keys, inclusion, exception, rule limit, runtime limit, and operation limit deterministically
  + wake emits only a candidate after exact task, plan, repository, capsule, policy, authority-evidence, lifecycle, and declared-requirement revalidation
  + Planner validates exact predecessor plan, repository generation, Calendar view, proof gates, recognized resources, CTPR graph, and objective dependency DAG
  + Planner selects ready objectives by declared numeric priority then stable SemanticId and returns a proposal only

& [ReplayAndDeterminism] are explicit
  + ordered maps and sets plus compact JSON produce one normalized snapshot form
  + restoration rejects malformed, unknown-field, invalid-digest, unsupported-version, and non-normalized input
  + replay applies a bounded sequence to the exact initial snapshot and returns the final snapshot plus every receipt
  + repeated replay of identical roots and operations is byte-equivalent
  + trace indexes are contiguous and operation identities cannot be admitted twice

& [BoundSet] is enforced
  + root bounds cover form records, payload bytes, operation bytes, emitted records, graph visits, recurrence occurrences, trace events, and replay operations
  + operation limits must be positive and no greater than the root envelope
  + graph, recurrence, input, emission, payload, record, trace, and replay exhaustion fail closed

& [DeliberateLimits] are binding
  + civil recurrence arithmetic is not implemented; supplied occurrence keys are evaluated under declared recurrence metadata
  + Calendar outputs candidates and does not commit, notify, synchronize, or execute
  + Planner recognizes resource identities but is not a capacity or optimization solver
  + repository state is in-memory only and no filesystem, Git, database, provider, network, process, thread, model, or hardware API is reachable
  + tandem lanes, Observer join, compiler correspondence, process procedures, live effects, and FPGA behavior remain separate slices

